# 📡️ P2-FG1: `StepSnapshot::encode_pack_with` wraps a `SemioEnvelope` header (`wrap_binary`,
# envelope id `stdio.step`, component `Pack`, version 1) around the UTF-8 bytes of
# `write_part21(&self.to_part21_document())` — the SAME Part-21 text the DSL facet emits. No packed
# binary layout of its own exists at this facet; text-native, same shape as json's own snapshot
# protocol (`framing record` + `chain payload utf8`). The SEMIO envelope itself is described ONCE,
# framework-side (`🧰️framework/…/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️.protocol.semio`) — this file
# describes ONLY the post-unwrap payload, per the recipe's own rule (cross-artifact `use` doesn't
# resolve at walk time yet).
dialect protocol
protocol stdio.step.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.step
start body

framing record
chain payload utf8
